    "lawSection": "Veterans' Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1242A\n\nSPONSOR: ADDABBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the veterans' services law, in relation to revising the\nNew York state veteran's memorial and monument registry\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation would require all New York veteran monuments and memo-\nrials to be included on the New York State Veterans Memorial Registry\nsite.\n\n \nSUMMARY OR PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends Section 29-a of the veterans' services law, as added\nby chapter 14 of the laws of 2023, so that: Subsection 1 changes the\nname of the Department of Veterans' Services' memorial registry site\nfrom New York Veterans Memorial Registry' to 'New York State Veteran's\nMemorial and Monument Registry.' Subsection 1 also states the registry\nis to be maintained by the Department of Veterans Services in collab-\noration with the director of the New York State Military Museum and\nVeterans Resource Center, the Commissioner of the Office of Parks,\nRecreation and Historic preservation, the Commissioner of the Office of\nGeneral Services and, the State Historian, and respective agencies and\nveteran organizations within New York towns, villages, counties and\ncities.\n\nSubsection 2 defines the parameters of the filterable database, includ-\ning details about the location, history, significance, specific veter-\nans, appropriate images, and other relevant information.\n\nSubsection 3 describes the manner in which the information and data are\nto be obtained from cities, counties, towns, villages, and other rele-\nvant organizations. Municipalities with a population with over a million\npeople will have no more than one year to submit requested information.\nMunicipalities with a population with less than one million will have\n120 days. The Department of Veterans' Services will have no more than 60\ndays to upload the received information to the website.\n\nSection two would set forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPrevious legislation (A9590/S8729 and A618/S843) were instrumental in\nthe implementation of a centralized database of veteran memorials, but\nit is limited. This legislation builds upon these pieces of legislation\nby requiring veteran monuments to be included in the registry and\nmandates a deadline for information to be submitted and uploaded to the\nsite. This legislation will create an exhaustive list of all veteran\nmemorials and monuments in New York State, resulting in the honoring of\nveterans, the education of the public, and the promotion of tourism.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2024: New Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
